---
description: Localisation — EN and ID at launch, any language as a locale pack
globs: ["src/**/*.tsx", "src/lib/i18n/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

"Any further language **without a code change**" is only true if no user-facing
string ever reaches a component.

- Every string through `t('key')`. That includes `placeholder`, `aria-label`,
  `title` and `alt` — assistive-technology strings are localised too.
- Keys are namespaced by screen: `client.overview.heroTitle`, not `heroTitle`.
- Locale files are **append-only across agents**. Add your keys to both
  `en.json` and `id.json`; never edit another agent's. This is the single most
  likely merge conflict in the project.
- Numbers, currency, dates and temperature come from the locale — **never string
  concatenation**. Indonesian renders `Rp 1.444,70`, separators inverted from
  the English default.
- **Design for the longer string.** Indonesian runs 20–30 % longer: "Needs
  cleaning" → "Perlu dibersihkan". Never size a control to its English label. No
  fixed `width` on anything containing text.
- Logical properties everywhere, so adding Arabic is a `dir` attribute rather
  than a rewrite. Mirror direction-indicating icons under RTL; do not mirror
  icons that depict objects.
- Voice input always has a text fallback and a visible transcript.

Review every component in **both** locales before calling it done. No tool
catches a truncation; you are the only check.
